# Verification before completion

Before a completion claim, identify the behavior that could fail and run the narrowest check that exercises it. Read the exit status and output. For a UI, CLI, or integration change, smoke-test the actual surface; tests alone do not prove the user-facing path works.

Report only checks actually run and what they proved. Separate untested paths and environmental blockers from verified behavior. Do not claim success from an edit, a test name, an agent report, or an inferred default.
